# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.stop() stops a sleeping strand tagged with that tag;
#         concurrent variants: stop before vs after strand starts sleeping.
# blocked: runtime — sleep(100ms) suspends indefinitely in REPL context; echo undefined at top level
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Reason (updated v0.13.5 probe):
#   Parse error FIXED by v0.13.5: `{expr} & stmt` now parses inside tag-scope
#   bodies.  New runtime blockers:
#     1. sleep(100ms) — in REPL mode the single loader strand suspends
#        indefinitely (no other strand to keep the scheduler alive); the
#        statement never resumes and produces nil.
#     2. echo("No") — `echo` is not defined at top level. Bare `echo` is
#        not a global alias; unqualified names inside closure bodies do not
#        resolve to Lobby methods (use Lobby.echo explicitly).
#   Redesign requires the ## host: driver or a test that avoids blocking sleep.
#
# Original urbiscript (blocked on runtime; redesign before re-activating):
# # var tag = Tag.new() | {};
# # tag: { {sleep(100ms); echo("No")} & tag.stop() };
# # tag: { tag.stop() & {sleep(100ms); echo("No")} };
